AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Special Envoy Xia, for your briefing.
The United States remains committed to the implementation of the DRC-Rwanda Peace Agreement, which President Trump is proud to have facilitated.
We fully expect the timely implementation of all elements of the Agreement to advance peace, stability, and prosperity in eastern DRC and the broader Great Lakes region.
Moreover, we expect the DRC and Rwanda to uphold their obligations not to engage in any hostile acts or rhetoric and to resolve disputes by peaceful means through the Joint Oversight Committee (JOC), which has held three meetings to date.
Colleagues, as you know, the Agreement also stood up the Joint Security Coordination Mechanism (JSCM), which, in its last meeting, discussed turning the agreed upon Concept of Operations into a concrete operational plan.
At the most recent JOC meeting, the DRC and Rwanda finalized the Operation Order submitted by the JSCM and confirmed October 1 as the start date for the Order.
At the JOC meeting, the DRC and Rwanda also committed to facilitate ICRC access to all detainees.
The United States would like to highlight our appreciation for the efforts of the African Union Facilitation, under the Republic of Togo, and the African Union Commission in working towards the implementation of this peace agreement.
Furthermore, we welcome Qatar’s ongoing efforts to mediate negotiations between the DRC and AFC/M23, and we continue to lend our full support to this effort. It is critical for the stability of eastern DRC, however, these negotiations reach a successful conclusion.
We expect the DRC and M23 to act in good faith in these negotiations and to uphold the Declaration of Principles which they have already signed and in which both sides committed to a permanent ceasefire.
The United States looks to all other armed groups to cease their killings and turn to peaceful means to resolve their differences.
The United States will hold accountable spoilers to peace and expect Council members to do the same.
And with that I thank you, Mr. President.
